PART 2: WHAT IS VITE?

================================================================================

Vite Definition

Vite, pronounced"veet", is a modern frontend build tool originally created by Evan You.

It provides tooling for development and production builds.

Key Features
Feature                  | Purpose
-------------------------|----------------------------------------------
Fast Development Start   | Starts the development environment quickly
HMR                      | Updates modules during development
Production Build         | Generates optimized production assets
ES Modules               | Uses modern JavaScript module concepts
Framework Support        | Supports React, Vue and other technologies
Configuration            | Provides useful defaults
TypeScript               | Supports TypeScript-based projects


================================================================================

VITE VS CREATE REACT APP - LESSON COMPARISON

================================================================================

Feature        | Create React App      | Vite
---------------|-----------------------|-------------------------
Startup        | Slower                | Faster
Hot Reload/HMR | Slower workflow       | Fast HMR
Build Tooling  | Older CRA approach    | Modern Vite approach
Configuration  | More CRA conventions  | Lightweight setup
Development    | Traditional CRA flow  | Modern dev-server flow


The exact speed, build size, and performance depend on the project, machine, dependencies, and Vite/CRA versions, so values such as "30-60 seconds vs 1-2 seconds" should be treated as lesson examples rather than guaranteed measurements.

