PART 4: PROJECT STRUCTURE

================================================================================

Typical Vite React Project
my-react-app/
│
├── node_modules/         → Installed packages
│
├── public/               → Static/public files
│
├── src/                  → Application source code
│   ├── App.jsx           → Main App component
│   ├── App.css           → App-specific styles
│   ├── main.jsx          → React entry point
│   ├── index.css         → Global styles
│   └── assets/           → Images/assets
│
├── index.html            → Main HTML document
├── package.json          → Project metadata/dependencies/scripts
├── package-lock.json     → Dependency lock file
├── vite.config.js        → Vite configuration, when present
└── .gitignore            → Git ignore rules

Folder/File Summary
File / Folder       | Purpose
--------------------|-----------------------------------------------
node_modules/       | Installed npm dependencies
public/             | Public/static assets
src/                | Main application source code
src/App.jsx         | Main React component
src/App.css         | Styles associated with App
src/main.jsx        | React application entry point
src/index.css       | Global CSS
src/assets/         | Source-managed images/assets
index.html          | HTML entry document
package.json        | Scripts, dependencies and project metadata
package-lock.json   | Locks resolved dependency versions
vite.config.js      | Vite configuration
.gitignore          | Files/directories Git should ignore


