KEY FILE: main.jsx

================================================================================

Example:

import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';

import App from './App.jsx';
import './index.css';

ReactDOM
  .createRoot(document.getElementById('root'))
  .render(
    <React.StrictMode>
      <App />
    </React.StrictMode>
  );

Code Explanation
Code / Concept                  | Purpose
--------------------------------|-----------------------------------------
import React                    | Imports React where needed by setup/code
react-dom/client                | Provides React DOM client APIs
import App                      | Imports main App component
import './index.css'            | Loads global CSS
document.getElementById('root') | Gets the root HTML element
ReactDOM.createRoot(...)        | Creates React root
<App />                         | Renders App component
React.StrictMode                | Enables additional development checks

Flow
index.html
    ↓
#root
    ↓
main.jsx
    ↓
createRoot()
    ↓
<App />
    ↓
React Application


================================================================================

KEY FILE: App.jsx

================================================================================

A starter template may look similar to:

import { useState } from 'react';

import reactLogo from './assets/react.svg';
import viteLogo from '/vite.svg';

import './App.css';

export default function App() {

  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <>

      <div>

        <a
          href="https://vitejs.dev"
          target="_blank"
        >
          <img
            src={viteLogo}
            className="logo"
            alt="Vite logo"
          />
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://react.dev"
          target="_blank"
        >
          <img
            src={reactLogo}
            className="logo react"
            alt="React logo"
          />
        </a>

      </div>

      <h1>Vite + React</h1>

      <div className="card">

        <button
          onClick={() =>
            setCount((count) => count + 1)
          }
        >
          count is {count}
        </button>

        <p>
          Edit <code>src/App.jsx</code>
          and save to test HMR
        </p>

      </div>

      <p className="read-the-docs">
        Click on the Vite and React logos to learn more
      </p>

    </>
  );
}

Code Explanation
Code / Concept                         | Purpose
---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------
useState                               | Imports React state Hook
useState(0)                            | Initializes count to 0
count                                  | Current count value
setCount                               | Updates count
onClick                                | Handles button click
setCount(count => count + 1)           | Increments count
return (...)                           | Describes component UI using JSX
reactLogo / viteLogo                   | Imported image assets
App.css                                | Component/application styles

Counter Flow
count = 0
   ↓
USER CLICKS
   ↓
setCount(count => count + 1)
   ↓
STATE CHANGES
   ↓
COMPONENT RE-RENDERS
   ↓
UPDATED COUNT DISPLAYED


