Step 5: Add State and Interactivity

================================================================================

import { useState } from 'react';

export default function App() {

  const [name, setName] =
    useState('');

  return (
    <>

      <h1>
        Welcome, {name || 'Guest'}!
      </h1>

      <input
        type="text"
        value={name}
        onChange={(e) =>
          setName(e.target.value)
        }
        placeholder="Enter your name"
      />

    </>
  );
}

Code Explanation
Code / Concept             | Purpose
---------------------------|---------------------------------------
useState('')               | Creates name state
name                       | Current input value
setName                    | Updates name state
value={name}               | Input value comes from React state
onChange                   | Runs when user changes input
e.target.value             | Current text entered by user
setName(e.target.value)     | Stores entered text
name || 'Guest'            | Shows Guest when name is empty

Flow
USER TYPES
    ↓
onChange
    ↓
e.target.value
    ↓
setName()
    ↓
STATE CHANGES
    ↓
COMPONENT RE-RENDERS
    ↓
Welcome, <name>!


